# Allowlist: the image is built from the package and the web assets it serves, nothing
# else. In particular no .env, no captures, downloads or CA material, no .venv, no .git.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!wx_dlh/
!web/inject.js
!web/dashboard.html
!web/dashboard.js
!scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh
# `*` only matches the top level, so `!wx_dlh/` on its own hands the builder every file
# below it - including the git-ignored output a native run leaves there when a directory
# setting points at the package tree (`WX_DLH_CAPTURE_DIR=wx_dlh/captures`: JSONL logs,
# .mitm flow archives, media). Docker takes the last matching pattern, so the tree is
# excluded again and only the modules come back. The package is pure Python and has no
# package data - tests/test_docker.py fails if that stops being true.
wx_dlh/**
!wx_dlh/*.py
# After every negation, so no allowlisted tree can re-admit them. Redundant today (the
# negations above name one file each, plus the package's own modules), kept because the
# next negation someone adds need not be that narrow.
**/__pycache__
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.cer
**/*.crt
**/*.key
**/*.p12
